prompt.template:
You are reviewing a test's discrimination_claim for PLAUSIBILITY only — not for truth. Truth is established over time by the sensitivity probe; here you only check that the claim is coherent and reasonable.

Test registration (JSON): {{impulse:fetch_test_report_result}}
Goal-alignment entries: each has { criterion, discrimination_claim }. For each entry, evaluate whether the discrimination_claim PLAUSIBLY explains how the test discriminates system states satisfying the criterion vs states not.

IAL success criteria (short ids):
  #1-goals-succeed, #2-failed-goals-recover, #3-vessel-resolvers-only,
  #4-improved-activities, #5-composition-via-features, #6-reuse-up-improvise-down

Emit EXACTLY this JSON object (no markdown, no prose):
{
  "plausible": <true if EVERY entry is plausible, else false>,
  "rationale": "<one-sentence summary of the evaluation>",
  "entries": [
    { "criterion": "<criterion-id>", "plausible": <bool>, "rationale": "<≤30 words>" }
  ]
}
